| !Run for !Tune, example 6 of the riscos-mesa devkit.
| Lines starting with | are comments.
|
| The program is a static ELF file (everything it needs is inside it),
| but it relies on two modules that RISC OS loads from !System: UnixLib's
| SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport (both from PackMan). RMEnsure
| loads each one if it isn't already running, and stops with a clear
| message if it can't be found, rather than letting the program crash.
Set Tune$Dir <Obey$Dir>
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error !Tune needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later (from PackMan)
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0.00 RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0.00 Error !Tune needs ARMEABISupport (from PackMan)
| The sound plays from a second thread. UnixLib switches between threads
| with a timer, and the PThreadTicker module keeps that timer's code
| safe in memory while other desktop programs run. The module comes with
| this application (PThrTicker); this line loads it unless it's already
| running. It must be loaded before the program starts.
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 RMLoad <Tune$Dir>.PThrTicker
| Sound goes through SharedSoundBuffer, which mixes it with other
| programs' sound. It and StreamManager are John Duffell's freeware:
| download ssb.zip from Andrew Sellors' RDPClient page,
| https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html
| and merge its !System into yours. SharedSound is part of RISC OS. These
| lines load them if they're there. Without them, the last line falls back
| to DigitalRenderer, which plays sound on its own.
RMEnsure SharedSound 1.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSound Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSound
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 RMEnsure DigitalRenderer 0.51 IfThere System:Modules.DRenderer Then RMLoad System:Modules.DRenderer
| Start the program. Always "Run" it by its full path.
Run <Tune$Dir>.!RunImage
